  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (1 of 6 used): all three witnesses pass, and the concept reads one atom, `kin.speed`.\n\n**The concept** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/complete_halt.lean`): the body is `.cmp (.measure \"kin_speed\" [a]) .le (.param \"speed_tol\")`. It holds when the road user's sampled speed is at or below the caller's tolerance at that observation. A speed exactly at the tolerance still counts as at rest, because the contract says \"at or below\". If the speed isn't observed, the result is unknown rather than false. The contract settles every choice, so there are no narrowings.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/complete_halt.lean`): the tolerance is set to 0.1 m/s, and each trace has three scenes, one per second.\n- **holds:** the speeds are 0, 0.1 m/s and 0, so the middle scene sits exactly on the tolerance.\n- **fails:** the vehicle creeps forward at 0.5 m/s.\n- **blind:** the same trace as holds, with `kin.speed` hidden, which gives unknown.\n\nThe record had nothing wrong with it. `task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
